# Topic Isolation Rule

This workspace organizes distinct learning topics under `topics/<topic-name>/` (e.g., `topics/git/`, `topics/dotnet/`).

## Agent Behavior Mandate:
1. **Isolation**: Every topic is self-contained. Never read, reference, cross-link, or leak learning records, mission items, or glossaries from one topic to another.
2. **Scoping**: When working on a topic (or invoking `/teach` / `/teachme`), resolve all relative paths (`MISSION.md`, `RESOURCES.md`, `GLOSSARY.md`, `lessons/`, `learning-records/`) strictly within `topics/<topic-name>/`.
3. **New Topics**: When a new topic is started, instantiate it from `topics/_template/` into `topics/<topic-name>/`.
